  "event_seq": 102,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume roughly doubled since August (E-05: 610→590→1180→1260/month) because the majority of disputed bills (1785 of 3025, E-02) are tied to ACTUAL meter reads, not estimate substitutions — ruling out tariff changes (E-01) and making AMI/field read-capture gaps insufficient as the dominant cause. Current evidence best supports that a change to billing import validation rules around August (H-BILLING-RULE-CHANGE) is causing otherwise-valid ACTUAL reads to be rejected or mishandled during billing import, producing incorrect bills that customers then dispute; a secondary minority of disputes (1240 ESTIMATED-read bills) is driven by a field-staffing route-completion shortfall (0.88 vs 0.95 target, E-03)."
