  "what": "problem PD-1@v2 drafted",
  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 116.0,
  "event_seq": 262,
  "root_problem": "Billing dispute ticket volume roughly doubled since August 2026 (610→590→1180→1260/month, E-05) because the billing-import high-consumption validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 (E-12), compares raw unscaled meter register values against 12-month m3 consumption history; since firmware v4.2 meters (rolled out June 2026) report readings in a register unit of 0.1 m3 rather than the m3 unit legacy firmware uses (E-13), BV-17 misclassifies legitimate v4.2 readings as high-consumption outliers and rejects them (REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION) at billing import. This rejection mechanism directly produced estimate substitution for 1184 of the 1240 disputed ESTIMATED-read bills (E-11, superseding the field-staffing explanation), and the same billing-import mechanism is also implicated in the bulk of the 1785 disputed ACTUAL-read bills (E-02 revised), so roughly 98% of disputed bills trace to this one BV-17/firmware unit-mismatch, driving customers to dispute the resulting incorrect bills."
 },
